# Email two-factor authentication (spec 047)
## Key the one-time codes are hashed under. Optional: falls back to AUTH_SECRET,
## which every deployment already sets. Codes are stored as an HMAC under this
## key, so a database dump alone cannot reveal them. Rotating it invalidates
## every code currently in flight (users simply request a new one).
# TWO_FACTOR_CODE_SECRET=
## The three numeric settings below take a POSITIVE WHOLE NUMBER. Anything else
## (a fraction, zero, a negative, or a non-number) falls back to the default
## rather than being coerced — `0.5` must not silently become `0`.
## Lifetime of a one-time sign-in code, in milliseconds. Default: 600000 (10 minutes).
TWO_FACTOR_CODE_TTL_MS=600000
## Consecutive failed code verifications before the account is locked out. Default: 5.
TWO_FACTOR_MAX_ATTEMPTS=5
## How long that lockout lasts, in milliseconds. Default: 900000 (15 minutes).
TWO_FACTOR_LOCK_MS=900000

# Email SMTP Service Configuration
SMTP_HOST=smtp.your-provider.com
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=your-smtp-username
SMTP_PASSWORD=your-smtp-password

